{
  "$description": "Venom Design System — accent dimension (2026-08-01 Vercel-style retheme). Five optional accents delivered as [data-accent=\"...\"] override blocks in the generated tokens/accents.css. Each block overrides ONLY the accent-derived custom properties (accent.*, text.on-accent, text.link*, border.focus, focus.ring, selection.*); everything else stays theme-owned. `data-accent` absent or \"mono\" keeps the base monochrome themes. Hex values are ported verbatim from the legacy Vercel-style stylesheet; `base` carries the venom-dark values (dark is the :root default theme) and `themes.venom-light` carries per-theme overrides where the legacy palette diverges (emerald and rose). venom-hc additionally re-pins focus.ring/border.focus to its own HC values in the generated CSS — accents never lower HC's focus guarantees.",
  "$notes": {
    "accent.active": "The legacy palette defines no pressed shade; the legacy hover value is reused for the active state (no invented colors).",
    "selection.bg": "The legacy soft focus-ring wash — rgba(accent, 0.2) — reused as the selection wash.",
    "selection.fg": "var(--text-primary) so selected text keeps the current theme's text color."
  },
